# Finder/iCloud duplicate files ("pipeline 2.py"): a SPACE, then the digit.
#
# Deliberately NOT `*2.py`. A digit suffix is how this project names a TOOL
# version, not a file revision, so that glob hid three modules the package
# imports and a fresh clone would have raised ImportError before any predictor
# ran. Those modules are now archcandy_v2.py / crossbeta_v2.py, which reads as a
# version and cannot collide with this rule; superseded code lives in
# legacy/runners/ with a `_deprecated` suffix instead of being ignored in place.
* [0-9].py
